# No dense layer on stack5 (stack5.bux: the factorial's candidate with the CPLM copy
# pointer and GatedNorm): its first layer's FFN routed like every other's, as
# dense0.bux routes the candidate's. On the candidate that left the loss as it was and
# took away most of the gradient's clipping, whose largest share came from the dense
# first layer's SwiGLU. Does it hold beside the pointer and GatedNorm? Everything else
# is stack5's, so it pairs with it by seed, and with the candidate.
use stack5

# 2023 Mixtral, 2025 Qwen3 MoE, gpt-oss: stack5's model with the first layer's FFN
# routed, as every other's; a layer of experts' capacity at the same active parameters,
# every layer alike.
stack5_d0 = embed
            gn_layer(hy_delta) gn_layer(hy_delta)^2 gn_layer(g_k(v=@v1))
            (gn_layer(hy_delta)^3 gn_layer(g_k(v=$v1)))^(layers // 4 - 1)
            fr_norm @h fr_out hy_mtp
model     = stack5_d0
